At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

Flix is a leading green mobility provider, connecting millions of travellers through a smart, tech-driven network. In India, we are building a fast-growing intercity bus network with local partner operators. The Finance team ensures accurate , compliant and timely financial reporting that supports this growth. &nbsp; We are looking for a hands-on Junior Accounting Manager to support day-to-day accounting operations and the monthly close for FlixBus India. You will own core accounting processes such as accounts payable, general ledger, reconciliations and statutory compliance support, working closely with the Finance team, Group Accounting and external advisors. &nbsp;

About the Role

• Prepare and review journal entries, accruals, prepayments and provisions as part of the monthly, quarterly and year-end close. &nbsp;

• Manage accounts payable and accounts receivable processes, including invoice verification, vendor payments and partner operator settlements. &nbsp;

• Perform bank, vendor, intercompany and balance sheet reconciliations, and follow up on open items. &nbsp;

• Ensure correct GST, TDS and other indirect and direct tax treatment; support timely filings and reconciliations (GSTR-2B vs books, TDS returns). &nbsp;

• Prepare MIS reports, variance analyses and schedules for management and Group reporting, including reporting under group accounting policies. &nbsp;

• Maintain fixed asset registers and support depreciation calculations. &nbsp;

• Support statutory, tax and internal audits by preparing schedules and responding to auditor queries. &nbsp;

• Maintain strong documentation and internal controls in line with company policies and the group control framework. &nbsp;

• Identify opportunities to improve and automate accounting processes using ERP features, Excel and reporting tools. &nbsp;

• Coordinate with Procurement, Operations, Revenue and external CAs/consultants for smooth finance operations. &nbsp;

About You

• Graduate (B.Com/BBA/BMS) or Postgraduate (M.Com/MBA Finance or equivalent) in Accounting/Finance. CA Inter, CMA Inter or equivalent qualifications are an added advantage.

• Minimum 3 years of hands-on experience in Accounting/Accounts Payable, with mandatory experience in Oracle ERP (preferably Oracle Fusion), ideally in a mid-to-large organisation. Experience in transportation, travel, e-commerce or technology sectors is preferred.

• Good understanding of Indian GAAP/Ind AS and Indian tax regulations, including TDS, Income Tax and GST.

• Strong technical proficiency in ERP and accounting systems, with advanced MS Excel skills (Pivot Tables, VLOOKUP/XLOOKUP, formulas and reconciliations). Working knowledge of PowerPoint and Outlook is required.

• Familiarity with TRACES, e-invoicing and e-way bill systems. Exposure to BI tools and process automation, such as Power BI and Power Query, is an added advantage.

• Strong attention to detail, accuracy and ownership, with the ability to manage tight deadlines, particularly during month-end and year-end closing.

• Strong analytical, problem-solving and process improvement skills, with clear written and verbal communication in English and the ability to collaborate with global, cross-functional teams.

• High integrity, confidentiality and a collaborative mindset, with the ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment.

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere : Depending on your role, work from another location for up

COMPANY

We are recruiting a position for a reference Big4 Consulting company located in Lisbon.﻿
CANDIDATE

The candidate to be hired will be responsible for:

• Manage multiple technical and advisory Tax Compliance projects to a wide range of domestic and global clients;

• Identify and develop new strategic business opportunities;

• Manage timings and expectations with customers;

• Deliver quality deliverables/solutions using general Tax Compliance knowledge and contribute to the profitable growth by ensuring client engagements are executed in an efficient manner by processes optimization and leveraging on technology;

• Advise local and multinational companies in order to align their tax compliance position with their business strategy in order to maintain competitive advantage and provide shareholder value;

• Ensure the submission of corporate tax obligations (IRC, IVA, IRS, IMI, etc), as as well as other compliance and reporting obligations (e.g. COPE and CBCR);

• Stay abreast of current tax, legal and business trends relevant to the client's business;

• Contribute to the teams good productivity and motivation with good communication and cooperation to guarantee the best result.

PROFILE

• Academic Degree in Tax, Economics or similar fields of study, mainly in reference university;

• At least 4 years of professional experience in Tax Compliance;

• Background in consulting environment, mainly in Big4 or Second Tier companies, is valued;

• Experience in team management;

• Full English proficiency.

Integration in a solid and company that offers a Competitive remuneration package and includes support for flexible working and career development
Candidates considered will be contacted within a maximum period of 10 working days.
